WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.347
Google's new Gemini model costs

00:00:02.147 --> 00:00:03.587
double per token,

00:00:03.387 --> 00:00:05.265
and the cheaper one catches

00:00:05.065 --> 00:00:06.067
up in January.

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:08.864
Hydrogen costs a dollar fifty

00:00:08.664 --> 00:00:10.615
per million input tokens,

00:00:10.415 --> 00:00:12.219
and seven fifty for output.

00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:13.648
That is twice the price

00:00:13.448 --> 00:00:15.024
of three point eight Flash.

00:00:15.574 --> 00:00:17.225
It launched November twelfth.

00:00:17.265 --> 00:00:18.671
Flash keeps its old price

00:00:18.471 --> 00:00:19.532
through December.

00:00:19.572 --> 00:00:21.104
From January first,

00:00:20.904 --> 00:00:22.156
both cost the same.

00:00:22.706 --> 00:00:24.823
On Google's command line agent

00:00:24.623 --> 00:00:27.737
test, Hydrogen scores fifty-seven percent

00:00:27.537 --> 00:00:29.577
to Flash's eighteen point two.

00:00:29.617 --> 00:00:31.671
An independent index rates it

00:00:31.471 --> 00:00:33.154
fifty-four to thirty-one.

00:00:33.704 --> 00:00:34.970
Per finished task,

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.154
it is already cheaper on

00:00:35.954 --> 00:00:36.924
this benchmark.

00:00:36.964 --> 00:00:38.601
Three dollars sixteen,

00:00:38.401 --> 00:00:40.690
against seven seventy-seven for Flash.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.125
Short calls can simply cost

00:00:42.925 --> 00:00:44.444
double until January.

00:00:44.484 --> 00:00:46.208
Long agent runs with many

00:00:46.008 --> 00:00:48.095
tool calls should save the most.

00:00:48.645 --> 00:00:50.323
Before you swap models,

00:00:50.123 --> 00:00:51.801
set thinking to medium,

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:53.548
because the default is now high.

00:00:53.588 --> 00:00:55.573
The old thinking budget returns

00:00:55.373 --> 00:00:56.036
an error.

00:00:56.076 --> 00:00:57.988
Thinking also counts toward your

00:00:57.788 --> 00:00:58.661
output limit.

00:00:59.211 --> 00:01:01.010
Explicit caching is gone,

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.077
and temperature is silently ignored.

00:01:03.117 --> 00:01:05.624
Hydrogen is a short-term release,

00:01:05.424 --> 00:01:06.740
so pin the model ID.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.896
Cost per finished task now

00:01:08.696 --> 00:01:10.112
tells you more than the

00:01:09.912 --> 00:01:10.687
price list.

00:01:10.727 --> 00:01:13.352
Test both models before January first.

00:01:13.902 --> 00:01:15.678
The full story has every

00:01:15.478 --> 00:01:17.411
API change to check before

00:01:17.211 --> 00:01:18.120
you switch.

